#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
omarchy-lock-studio — a safe, Omarchy-way lock screen customizer.

* Writes into whichever lock-screen service the shell actually runs — the
  enabled clone of omarchy.lock (omaFace, or a plain <you>.lock clone) — never
  /usr/share/omarchy, and never into a plugin the shell has disabled.
* Generates LockView.qml from a template, preserving the password field + PAM
  auth signals (so you can always unlock), and reads the host Service.qml so a
  property added by an Omarchy/omaFace update is carried instead of breaking the
  view. A post-update hook re-applies it, so big updates no longer break it.
* Serves a local UI in its own desktop window (WebKitGTK; Firefox is the
  fallback) with a real-time preview that uses your active Omarchy theme colors.
* Shows one New King James verse per clock hour on the lock screen; the verse
  turns over on the hour and needs no network.
* Backs up LockView.qml before every change; supports restore + restore-stock.

Controls:
  omarchy-lock-studio            start server + open the app window
  omarchy-lock-studio --app      force the app window
  omarchy-lock-studio --browser  force a browser tab instead
  omarchy-lock-studio --no-open  start server without opening anything
  omarchy-lock-studio --restore-stock   restore the untouched cloned lock
  omarchy-lock-studio --sync            re-apply the saved settings to the
                                        active lock plugin (used by the
                                        post-update hook); add --restart to
                                        reload the shell afterwards
  omarchy-lock-studio --sync-repo       copy this app into a checkout of its
                                        project repo and push it there. Needs
                                        LOCKSTUDIO_REPO set to that checkout;
                                        the web UI button appears only then.
"""

